This is a simple backup of the packages used to interface with ROS2 humble packages and Nav2 framework.

This backup folder DOES NOT CONTAIN all the packages/files needed to run and requires installation of ROS2 humble, TurtleBot3 packages, and Nav2 packages

How to run demo
1. The folder name cannot contain any brackets "()"
2. Open the folder in command line and run the codes:
	a) colcon build --symlink-install
	b) . install/setup.bash
	c) ros2 launch turtlebot3_gazebo my_world.launch.py
3. Open a new terminal in the same folder and run the codes:
	a) ros2 launch tb3_nav2_commander bringup.launch.py map:=./map.yaml
4. Open a new terminal and run the code
	a) rviz2
5. In rviz2 gui, press the following buttons:
	a) add
	b) By topic
	c) /global_costmap/costmap/Map
6. Repeat step 5 for:
	a) /local_costmap/costmap/Map
	b) /plan/Path
7. For robot pose press
	a) add
	b) By display type
	c) TF
8. To have top down view press
	a) on the right side of rviz2 gui press Orbit (rviz_default_plugin)
	b) down down menu should appear
	c) press top down ortho
9. You can now set the 2D goal pose for navigation demo
